{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1979","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Fixing a Binary String"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a binary string $$$s$$$ of length $$$n$$$, consisting of zeros and ones. You can perform the following operation "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"exactly once"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Choose an integer $$$p$$$ ($$$1 \\le p \\le n$$$). "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Reverse the substring $$$s_1 s_2 \\ldots s_p$$$. After this step, the string $$$s_1 s_2 \\ldots s_n$$$ will become $$$s_p s_{p-1} \\ldots s_1 s_{p+1} s_{p+2} \\ldots s_n$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Then, perform a cyclic shift of the string $$$s$$$ to the left $$$p$$$ times. After this step, the initial string $$$s_1s_2 \\ldots s_n$$$ will become $$$s_{p+1}s_{p+2} \\ldots s_n s_p s_{p-1} \\ldots s_1$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, if you apply the operation to the string "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"110001100110"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" with $$$p=3$$$, after the second step, the string will become "},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"011"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"001100110"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", and after the third step, it will become "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"001100110"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"011"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A string $$$s$$$ is called "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$k$$$-proper"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if two conditions are met:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$s_1=s_2=\\ldots=s_k$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$s_{i+k} \\neq s_i$$$ for any $$$i$$$ ($$$1 \\le i \\le n - k$$$). "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, with $$$k=3$$$, the strings "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"000"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"111000111"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"111000"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" are $$$k$$$-proper, while the strings "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"000000"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"001100"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1110000"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" are not."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given an integer $$$k$$$, which "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"is a divisor"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of $$$n$$$. Find an integer $$$p$$$ ($$$1 \\le p \\le n$$$) such that after performing the operation, the string $$$s$$$ becomes $$$k$$$-proper, or determine that it is impossible. Note that if the string is initially $$$k$$$-proper, you still need to apply exactly one operation to it."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test consists of multiple test cases. The first line contains one integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^4$$$) — the number of test cases. The description of the test cases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$k$$$ ($$$1 \\le k \\le n$$$, $$$2 \\le n \\le 10^5$$$) — the length of the string $$$s$$$ and the value of $$$k$$$. It is guaranteed that $$$k$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"is a divisor"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of $$$n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each test case contains a binary string $$$s$$$ of length $$$n$$$, consisting of the characters "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$2 \\cdot 10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output a single integer — the value of $$$p$$$ to make the string $$$k$$$-proper, or $$$-1$$$ if it is impossible."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If there are multiple solutions, output any of them."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n7\n8 4\n11100001\n4 2\n1110\n12 3\n111000100011\n5 5\n00000\n6 1\n101001\n8 4\n01110001\n12 2\n110001100110\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n-1\n7\n5\n4\n-1\n3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, if you apply the operation with $$$p=3$$$, after the second step of the operation, the string becomes "},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"111"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"00001"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", and after the third step, it becomes "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"00001"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"111"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". This string is $$$4$$$-proper."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, it can be shown that there is no operation after which the string becomes $$$2$$$-proper."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third test case, if you apply the operation with $$$p=7$$$, after the second step of the operation, the string becomes "},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1000111"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"00011"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", and after the third step, it becomes "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"00011"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1000111"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". This string is $$$3$$$-proper."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the fourth test case, after the operation with any $$$p$$$, the string becomes $$$5$$$-proper."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"1979D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1979/problem/D"}